<header class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">Interactive research dashboard</div><h1>Used-Car Cost & Forecast Explorer</h1><div class="sub">Explore purchase-price and insurance estimates, compare scenarios, and change how vehicles are ranked. All calculations run in your browser using the source data packaged with this page.</div></div><div class="pill" id="dataStatus">Loading dataset…</div></header>
<section class="controls"><div class="field"><label for="horizon">Forecast view</label><select id="horizon"><option value="current">Current estimates</option><option value="5">5-year forecast</option><option value="10">10-year forecast</option></select></div><div class="field"><label for="scenario">Forecast scenario</label><select id="scenario"><option>Baseline</option><option>Optimistic</option><option>High-cost</option></select></div><div class="field"><label for="metric">Rank vehicles by</label><select id="metric"><option value="combined">Combined cost</option><option value="price">Purchase price</option><option value="insurance">Insurance cost</option><option value="monthly">Monthly insurance</option></select></div><div class="field search"><label for="search">Find a make or model</label><input id="search" placeholder="Search vehicles…"></div></section>
<section class="stats"><div class="stat"><small>Vehicles matched to insurance history</small><strong id="count">—</strong></div><div class="stat"><small>Lowest-cost vehicle in this view</small><strong id="winner">—</strong></div><div class="stat"><small>Lowest estimated combined cost</small><strong id="winnerCost">—</strong></div></section>
<section class="layout"><article class="card"><h2 id="chartTitle">Lowest combined cost</h2><div class="chart" id="chart"></div></article><article class="card"><h2>Selected model details</h2><div class="field"><label for="vehicle">Vehicle</label><select id="vehicle"></select></div><div id="details"></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">Insurance history</h2><div id="history"></div><div class="notice">Insurance values of zero in the source data are treated as missing observations, not free insurance. A proxy match uses a related/base-model record and is identified below.</div></article></section>
<section class="card tablewrap"><h2>Vehicle rankings <span class="match">· click a column heading to sort</span></h2><table><thead><tr><th data-sort="rank">Rank</th><th data-sort="name">Vehicle</th><th data-sort="match">Insurance record</th><th data-sort="price">Purchase price</th><th data-sort="monthly">Monthly insurance</th><th data-sort="insurance">5-year insurance</th><th data-sort="combined">Combined estimate</th><th data-sort="trend">Insurance trend / year</th></tr></thead><tbody id="tableBody"></tbody></table></section>
<section class="card assumptions"><h2>How the forecast works</h2><ol><li><b>Purchase price:</b> current average used price is grown by 2.5% general inflation plus a scenario-specific real used-car-market change. The price dataset is a cross-section, not a time series, so it does not claim to estimate model-specific historical price trends.</li><li><b>Insurance trend:</b> a log-linear annual trend is estimated from nonzero monthly observations, blending full history (65%) and recent 24 months (35%). Estimates are capped between −10% and +20% per year.</li><li><b>Forecast blend:</b> the observed model-specific trend receives 40% weight; the remaining 60% comes from the long-run scenario assumption.</li><li><b>Forecast cost:</b> at the selected future date, estimated purchase price is combined with the following five years of insurance, with insurance growing year by year.</li><li><b>Matching:</b> exact vehicle matches are preferred. A related/base-model proxy is labeled and should be treated as an estimate, not a trim-specific premium.</li></ol><p id="scenarioNotes"></p><p>These are scenario projections, not precise predictions. The model does not include vehicle condition, mileage, fuel/charging, maintenance, taxes, financing, driver profile, or location-specific insurance.</p></section>
